        "claim": "The policy would introduce an aggravating factor for murders in the context of 'rough sex' to prevent lighter sentences.",
        "evidence_id": "M",
        "quote": "introduce an aggravating factor for murders in the context of 'rough sex' to prevent it being used as an excuse for lighter sentences"
      },
      {
        "tier": "measurable",
        "claim": "The existing sentencing framework did not adequately reflect the seriousness of domestic abuse preceding homicides, according to a formal review.",
        "evidence_id": "E3",
        "quote": "the existing sentencing framework did not adequately reflect the seriousness of domestic abuse preceding homicides"
      },
      {
        "tier": "measurable",
        "claim": "Over 90% of domestic murder cases reviewed involved men killing their female partners or ex-partners, showing a clear gendered pattern.",
        "evidence_id": "E11",
        "quote": "Over 90% of domestic murder cases reviewed by Clare Wade KC involved men killing their female partners or ex-partners"
      },
      {
        "tier": "measurable",
        "claim": "An existing disparity means domestic murderers who use a weapon already in the home typically start at a 15-year sentence, versus 25 years if a weapon was brought to the scene.",
        "evidence_id": "E9",
        "quote": "bringing a weapon to a crime scene currently carries a 25-year starting point for murder, while using a weapon already present in the home (common in domestic homicides) typically starts at 15 years"
      },
